    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c6d8bf59_bc116e08",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T13:00:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The Virt APEX already needs to be updated in lockstep with pvmfw - if nothing else, crosvm is in the Virt APEX.\nAnd Rialto also lives in the Virt APEX.",
      "parentUuid": "99b2467f_362e3c2e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "c5d06568551777db46a2668cc6b120175c174ab3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e3dafb1_2785269a",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T13:06:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mmm, that\u0027s possible if we only hash the unsigned kernel, integrate the salt and use sha256. Since this only serves to recognize the service VM. We can just hash the unsigned kernel and compare it with `verified_boot_data.kernel_digest`.",
      "parentUuid": "c99d8725_0430cb1a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "c5d06568551777db46a2668cc6b120175c174ab3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0175e14_d3ea44b3",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T13:06:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The service VM/RKP VM is supposed to be hardcoded and it will be bundled with pvmfw, so that we can leverage the trust of pvmfw to the service VM.\n\n\u003e Instead of hard-coding a hash into pvmfw, can\u0027t we use a vbmeta property to tag the image as a service VM?\n\nI don\u0027t think so. As we want to leverage the trust of pvmfw to service VM, it\u0027s not secure with a vbmeta property, anyone can add a property and claim to be the service VM.",
      "parentUuid": "99b2467f_362e3c2e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "c5d06568551777db46a2668cc6b120175c174ab3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d47aa902_e065cc94",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T13:26:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, please, as this patch currently makes pvmfw hash the kernel twice (once in `verify_payload` then again in `is_service_vm`).",
      "parentUuid": "3e3dafb1_2785269a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "c5d06568551777db46a2668cc6b120175c174ab3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f888d1f_02a40c7f",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T13:26:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "pvmfw was always intended to be as payload-agnostic as possible but this does the exact opposite and IMO sends out the wrong signal to vendors. Instead, I\u0027d rather see us use a scalable design that gives some payloads more privileges (it\u0027s not clear from this patch what that would be for the service VM).\n\nHaving said that, if we\u0027re in a hurry to merge this patch, we can always rework the interface/specification later.\n\n\u003e anyone can add a property and claim to be the service VM.\n\nIsn\u0027t the property covered by AVB?",
      "parentUuid": "b0175e14_d3ea44b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "c5d06568551777db46a2668cc6b120175c174ab3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b05fd69a_8b4e4c06",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-25T13:36:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027re not actually trying to give the service VM extra privilege, it\u0027s important for the attestation that pvmfw confirms (via the DICE chain) that this is the one true service VM.\nI mentioned you on the design doc, would be interested in your comments.",
      "parentUuid": "6f888d1f_02a40c7f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 64
      },
